<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 57,353 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 57,353 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 57,353 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 58,554 tonnes on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			26,202	    26,749</p>
<p>    Import cargo			31,151	    31,805</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, four ships are expected to sail and nine to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		 60,000	 New Tatina		11/6</p>
<p>High speed disel    56,000	 Al-Maqwa		  11/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		10,000	 Wawasan Courage	 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		 9,300	 Vi Vi		     12/6</p>
<p>Palm oil		 4,000	 United Tina	     13/6</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
